<chapter xml:id="ch-when-farmers-manage" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>When Farmers Manage the Research</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      Farmer involvement changes which options are compared, how they are managed, what performance means and how results are interpreted. Roger's reconsideration of the strip-plot design gives this a concrete expression. Tricot contributes manageable comparisons across many farms, reporting and feedback. Differences in farmers' management can become part of the enquiry.
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <section xml:id="sec-when-farmers-manage-source-notes">
    <title>Source notes</title>
    <p>
      <alert>Main transcripts:</alert> On-farm Agricultural Trials; Multimethod Agricultural Research.
    </p>
    <p>
      <alert>Supporting:</alert> Controls; Measurements; CRFS Proxy Variables; RMS and Interactions; RMS and Multilevel Data.
    </p>
  </section>
</chapter>
